WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:34.030
<b>The Will of Ohara</b>

3
00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.900
900 years ago?

4
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.780
What?

5
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.810
Oh come on, that's ridiculous!

6
00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.010
You're saying they had a city
this futuristic, way back in the past?

7
00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:43.640
Well, it's only a theory.

8
00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:47.470
But there was a man I knew who
risked his life for archaeology.

9
00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.990
He shed light
on an ancient kingdom.

10
00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.970
We found an advanced machine
with a manufacture date that would coincide

11
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.710
with the reign
of that kingdom.

12
00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:04.490
This ancient machine... could it be that
it was made during the blank century?

13
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.470
So you do have some
knowledge of it.

14
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.750
Robin!

15
00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.170
You've heard
about this before?

16
00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:14.210
I'm sure this is a rather
painful subject for you.

17
00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.110
One that harkens
back to Ohara.

18
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:21.620
22 years ago, the Navy made
a Buster Call and destroyed your home.

19
00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.920
I believe this happened because the scholars
of Ohara learned of the existence

20
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.800
of that kingdom.

21
00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.670
Which was once
lost to history.

22
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:37.840
What's known as the blank century is a 100
year void during which a war was waged

23
00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.080
between an advanced civilization
and an alliance of 20 kingdoms.

24
00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.080
The 20 kingdoms
won the war.

25
00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:58.250
Later, they founded the World Government,
which has ruled ever since.

26
00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.350
And in order to prevent anyone from
inheriting that ancient kingdom's ideology.

27
00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:06.740
They erased every last
trace of it from history.

28
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.090
What?

29
00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.280
That's insane!

30
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.250
No way!

31
00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:14.210
So there's no
record of it at all?

32
00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:17.740
It must have been the greatest
story in the world!

33
00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.600
Hold on a second, Vegapunk!

34
00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.370
Ohara was destroyed because they
found out about this stuff, right?

35
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.540
So that means... anyone
else who learns about it...

36
00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.770
...will be erased, yes.

37
00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.320
Ahhhhhh!

38
00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.830
Excuse me!

39
00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.620
Then why did you
tell us, you asshole!

40
00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.640
It's too late!

41
00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:38.290
I know too much!

42
00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.730
I'm gonna get
blank Century!

43
00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.470
I need to forget!

44
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:44.050
Forget!

45
00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.090
Come on, you!

46
00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.150
Come on, you
stupid brain cells!

47
00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.530
Please, calm down.

48
00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.200
As I said, it's only a theory.

49
00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.570
I can't calm down!

50
00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.450
I'm about to get
murdered!

51
00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.870
Let me ask you, Nico Robin...

52
00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:01.880
If Ohara was indeed destroyed
because of this theory...

53
00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:06.060
...wouldn't that mean that the government
has essentially admitted that it's true?

54
00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.770
In what capacity are you
speaking right now, Vegapunk?

55
00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.650
Your employers
caused all this.

56
00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:12.860
They wiped out
the scholars of Ohara.

57
00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.300
Don't you know it's true?

58
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.950
With a position as high as yours,
wouldn't the government tell you?

59
00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.720
They didn't say a word.

60
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.360
The rule still stands.

61
00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.870
Even if I am affiliated with the government,
I would still be killed

62
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:26.010
for speaking of this.

63
00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:26.890
Huh?

64
00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:29.540
I don't wanna know!

65
00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.930
This is psychological
torture, you sicko!

66
00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.850
You damned us all!

67
00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.660
If that's so, then how?

68
00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:37.690
How did you find out
about the kingdom?

69
00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.980
The books that Ohara collected
in their library are gone!

70
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:41.960
They burned.

71
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.380
The will of Ohara lives on.

72
00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.830
That day, the world was thrown into
confusion.

73
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.790
Ohara was an island of scholars, revered
for its unparalleled collection of knowledge.

74
00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.730
Yet it was destroyed overnight,
leaving just one girl behind.

75
00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:06.350
They were accused of being a group
of fanatics, plotting to overthrow the

76
00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:07.580
government itself.

77
00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:14.180
Several months after the incident,
I visited Ohara myself.

78
00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.940
I was fond
of the great archaeologist,

79
00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.690
Professor Clover,
who had met an untimely demise.

80
00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.060
I wanted to pay my respects.

81
00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:24.090
You knew Professor Clover?

82
00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.360
Indeed.

83
00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.600
He was obsessed
with the 100-year void.

84
00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:35.220
He sailed the seas, scouring every corner
of the world for documents about it.

85
00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:40.630
He was arrested and jailed by the Navy ten
times, but they simply couldn't hold him.

86
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:43.410
There he is!

87
00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:44.630
Hey!

88
00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:49.350
Thanks to these tales, he soon became
the most famous archaeologist in the world.

89
00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:54.290
It was no surprise that scholars came
together in Ohara to join his quest.

90
00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.830
Soon, the island became
the holy land for archaeology.

91
00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.650
You could say his brilliance
was the cause of his death.

92
00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:06.860
The devastation in Ohara
shook me to the core.

93
00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.730
Nothing but scorched
earth remained.

94
00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.350
The once mighty tree
of knowledge was felt.

95
00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.390
Its resting place was a sea
of ash and desolation.

96
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:22.680
As if in a daze, I walked
deeper into the island.

97
00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.070
Then suddenly, I saw
something that stunned me.

98
00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.620
What is all of this?

99
00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.040
A vast number of books
on every subject

100
00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:36.030
were submerged in the lake
at the center of Ohara.

101
00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:41.060
The brave scholars must have struggled
to the last second, protecting their legacy

102
00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.990
as the Buster Call
rained down.

103
00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:46.100
This was their parting
gift to the future.

104
00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.330
Although Ohara had burned, it endured
in the only way that truly mattered.

105
00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:56.910
Even if marines happened upon the books,
they would be ignorant of their value.

106
00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.160
Ohara was victorious.

107
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:04.410
When I saw it, I couldn't
stop my tears from falling.

108
00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.590
I'll be all right.

109
00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.100
But I need you to take care
of Robin for me, please.

110
00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:10.910
But why?

111
00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.380
What about you?

112
00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:14.400
Aren't you going
to come with me?

113
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.080
Over here, are you...

114
00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.470
I can't leave yet.

115
00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.500
There's still
something left to do.

116
00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.200
No, Mom!

117
00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:24.900
You can't leave me now!

118
00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:26.870
I want to stay with you!

119
00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:28.160
Robin...

120
00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:31.580
History is mankind's
greatest treasure.

121
00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.940
As a scholar, you know this.

122
00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.350
Protect the books!

123
00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:37.630
Open up the library!

124
00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:39.640
Save as many as you can!

125
00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:43.060
We weren't trying to uncover
some dark secret.

126
00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:45.400
We wanted to hear
the voices of the past.

127
00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.090
We wanted to protect them.

128
00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.700
Our research ends here.

129
00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.150
But time marches on, even
if Ohara is destroyed.

130
00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:58.270
And as we believe in the past,
we also believe in the future that you

131
00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.050
will inherit.

132
00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:01.630
What does that mean?

133
00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.950
Someday, you will know.

134
00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.620
Saul, take her and go!

135
00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:17.350
Are you sure about this?

136
00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:18.880
I am.

137
00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:25.340
Mommy!

138
00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.420
You must live, Robin!

139
00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:37.290
Be proud, Robin!

140
00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.430
Your mom is
a wonderful woman!

141
00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.390
Ohara is a wonderful place!

142
00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.840
Never forget that!

143
00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.030
It's up to you to pass it on!

144
00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.840
Always remember...

145
00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.130
Ohara fought
against the world!

146
00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.810
Robin, are you crying?

147
00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.040
Jerk!

148
00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.000
How dare you make her cry
like that, bucket-head!

149
00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.110
I'm gonna give you
a piece of my mind!

150
00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:06.480
Get these shoes off me!

151
00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.010
Hey, are you even listening?

152
00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.520
You're right, Vegapunk.

153
00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.440
It's just as you guessed.

154
00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:23.660
Ohara uncovered
the existence of the kingdom.

155
00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:24.900
I see.

156
00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.210
The books in the lake.

157
00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.980
Where are they now?

158
00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.970
I wanted to bring them back
to Punk Hazard, of course.

159
00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.940
But if the higher-ups found out,
I feared that everything would be lost.

160
00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:40.090
Fortunately, that day, I wasn't
the only person there in Ohara.

161
00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.230
<b>22 Years Ago

Ohara
West Blue</b>

162
00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:48.110
<b>Several Months After
the Buster Call</b>

163
00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:05.400
I never thought I'd find
someone else here.

164
00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.130
Alright, pull it up!

165
00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.270
Giants!

166
00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:14.920
But why are they here?

167
00:10:15.670 --> 00:10:19.060
Do they have any idea how
valuable those books are?

168
00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:20.650
No!

169
00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:21.430
Wait!

170
00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:23.430
They, taking them!

171
00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:26.150
There's no point hiding.

172
00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:29.970
That head of yours sticks
out like a sore thumb.

173
00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:41.490
Hello, Vegapunk.

174
00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:42.640
It's been a while.

175
00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:45.750
<b>Monkey D. Dragon (Age 33)
Leader of the Freedom Fighters</b>

176
00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:47.520
Dragon!

177
00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:52.590
Now that I get a closer look,
it seems you've hit another growth spurt.

178
00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:56.970
<b>Dr. Vegapunk (Age 43)
Head of the Punk Hazard Lab</b>

179
00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.600
Never mind my head.

180
00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.710
What are you doing here?

181
00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:03.700
I could ask you the same
question, nice flowers.

182
00:11:04.210 --> 00:11:07.700
Seems I'm not the only one
who's mourning Professor Clover.

183
00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.950
You as well, small world.

184
00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:14.920
But, said again, he was quite
the adventurer in his youth.

185
00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:19.260
That nonsense about him
trying to destroy the world.

186
00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.340
The government was creative.

187
00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:23.070
I know.

188
00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.200
You must be wondering
what those giants are doing.

189
00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.860
The books are priceless.

190
00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:33.600
They can't allow just
anyone to take them away.

191
00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.930
Don't worry, I've already
checked them out.

192
00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.470
They're not bandits.

193
00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.350
They're not?

194
00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:42.520
They came here from Elbaph.

195
00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.800
[DRAGON] They know what
treasures they're holding.

196
00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.510
I spoke to their captain.

197
00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:55.060
He's a strange man
with bandages all over his body.

198
00:11:55.790 --> 00:12:00.020
He said, Ohara gave their lives
to save their legacy.

199
00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.490
I won't let it be
erased from history.

200
00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.350
Imagine if your government friends
found out about those books.

201
00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.860
They're gonna unleash
hell when you tell them.

202
00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:18.950
They know what?

203
00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:20.980
I'm not going to tell them.

204
00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:22.680
I was making a joke.

205
00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:26.590
But thank you for confirming
my suspicion that you're their dog.

206
00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:27.500
Hmm.

207
00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.730
It was naive of me to think you
joined my freedom fighters.

208
00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.300
Of course I won't!

209
00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:37.540
My mind would be wasted
on your penniless army.

210
00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:41.230
An inventor without funds
is like a horse without legs.

211
00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.110
Yeah, I got it?

212
00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.890
As cold and practical
as ever, I see.

213
00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.620
The World Government is
a massive organization.

214
00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:52.450
You can find sympathetic ears,
especially in the Navy.

215
00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:54.640
We have to keep
our eyes on the target.

216
00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:55.840
You know that.

217
00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:57.660
Of course I do.

218
00:12:59.480 --> 00:13:01.870
But this incident hit me hard.

219
00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.960
Those scholars were harmless.

220
00:13:05.040 --> 00:13:08.960
All they did was ask questions
in the face of an unreasonable law.

221
00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:11.560
And the government
burned them for it.

222
00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:17.200
I'll just have to start
a fire of my own.

223
00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.420
I always thought
you despised war.

224
00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.060
This broken world
must change.

225
00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:24.960
And I'll be the one to do it.

226
00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.430
In memory of Clover... for.

227
00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:29.500
For all of Ohara... I.

228
00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.310
I will press on.

229
00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:36.870
[SHAKA] Later that year, Dragon
bolstered his forces.

230
00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:39.330
Recruited Emporio Ivankov.

231
00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.210
And Bartholomew Kuma,

232
00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:46.040
To form
the Revolutionary Army,

233
00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:49.530
And they've shaken
the world ever since.

234
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.780
I can totally see why!

235
00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:56.020
He sounds awesome!

236
00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:57.150
Back up for a second!

237
00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.100
You said those giants
came from Elbaph?

238
00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:01.750
To think Dragon and Professor
Clover were friends.

239
00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.290
And I never had a clue.

240
00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.670
Evil, huh?

241
00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.020
So he joined up with Luffy's
dad right from the start?

242
00:14:08.020 --> 00:14:11.260
I feel like my brain's
gonna explode!

243
00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:12.700
None of this makes sense!

244
00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:14.820
Why did Kuma help
us two years ago?

245
00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.660
You're the one
who modified him!

246
00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.610
Can't you at least
tell us something?

247
00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:24.090
The Books of Ohara must be kept out
of the government's hands at any cost.

248
00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:35.070
Still, I could not resist making
the trip to Elbaph in secret.

249
00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.970
I read every last
document there.

250
00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:46.340
And now, the mystery
that Ohara unraveled...

251
00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.460
...lives on in my brain.

252
00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:53.760
I've been continuing their research
in secret to this very day.

253
00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.470
Vegapunk, I have a question.

254
00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.940
The Giant
captain you mentioned...

255
00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:02.700
Dad!

256
00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:09.170
It's Saul, isn't it?

257
00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:13.670
[SHAKA] He's in hiding now.

258
00:15:15.380 --> 00:15:17.200
No one else
can know the truth.

259
00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.460
Thank you, Doctor Vegapunk.

260
00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:29.530
You've kept the dream
of Ohara alive.

261
00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.080
I can never repay you.

262
00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:32.880
You need not thank me...

263
00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:35.110
...for pursuing all
branches of knowledge.

264
00:15:35.190 --> 00:15:36.900
That is the way of a scholar.

265
00:15:48.900 --> 00:15:52.480
Where are these crazy
future shoes taking me?

266
00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.860
I'm afraid I can't release you.

267
00:15:58.940 --> 00:16:00.170
But do come along.

268
00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:02.580
There's something
I need you to see.

269
00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.130
They really hid
this robot's cockpit, huh?

270
00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:06.990
<b>Scrap Heap
Fabriophase
Egghead</b>

271
00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:08.600
Wait a sec.

272
00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:10.990
What if the robot
doesn't need one?

273
00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.180
What if it's self-piloting?

274
00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:14.600
Let's try talking to it.

275
00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:15.640
It might activate.

276
00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.380
Okay, let's see.

277
00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:19.160
Robot!

278
00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:20.440
Get up and go!

279
00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:23.570
Aw, nope.

280
00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.430
Wonder if there's a password.

281
00:16:25.510 --> 00:16:26.340
No way.

282
00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.970
We just need its name.

283
00:16:28.050 --> 00:16:29.410
I'll guess it easy.

284
00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:30.710
Wake up!

285
00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.380
Robobert!

286
00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:36.460
Robonoski!

287
00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:37.640
Come on.

288
00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.030
Oh, come on!

289
00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:39.400
What are you, like five?

290
00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:42.070
This thing doesn't work
like a freaking toy.

291
00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:49.510
No way!

292
00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:04.300
Is everyone all right?

293
00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:05.730
I'm fine.

294
00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:06.570
Oh no!

295
00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.350
Robobert, did you explode?

296
00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:09.360
No.

297
00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.140
That wasn't an explosion.

298
00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:13.280
But then, what
in the world was it?

299
00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:15.460
Help!

300
00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:17.510
Huh?

301
00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.530
I request a help!

302
00:17:20.610 --> 00:17:21.610
Hm?

303
00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:22.150
Wait.

304
00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:22.850
Quasar?

305
00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:23.810
Oh zounds!

306
00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:25.940
I've made a terrible mistake.

307
00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:27.650
I request a help, please!

308
00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:29.020
Uh...

309
00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:31.730
Did space-time distort
while I was warping?

310
00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:34.080
Was that old man
there before?

311
00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.330
I don't think so.

312
00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:35.880
No.

313
00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:36.590
Hey!

314
00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.290
Something like a fresh egg!

315
00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:38.650
No!

316
00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:45.350
I don't really get
what's going on.

317
00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:46.690
Okay, old man.

318
00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:47.960
I'll see what I can do.

319
00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.610
Please, my dear boy.

320
00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:55.810
Get me out of here!

321
00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:56.940
Wait a sec.

322
00:17:57.350 --> 00:17:59.590
This is just like when
I met Kin'emon.

323
00:18:01.900 --> 00:18:02.980
Quickly, now!

324
00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.470
Quickly!

325
00:18:07.170 --> 00:18:08.450
It really is!

326
00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:09.360
Oh!

327
00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:15.550
I thought so.

328
00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:16.560
It's him!

329
00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:17.440
Oh!

330
00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:19.710
Thank you.

331
00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.910
You're Dragon's son, I believe.

332
00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.440
I heard that you'd
arrived here.

333
00:18:24.520 --> 00:18:26.110
You and your friends.

334
00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.590
And you are?

335
00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:29.160
Bonney!

336
00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.440
You're all grown up!

337
00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.060
Doctor Vegapunk!

338
00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:35.410
And the picture of him!

339
00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:36.570
Old man!

340
00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:37.190
Can you...

341
00:18:37.190 --> 00:18:37.990
Fly?!

342
00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:38.900
You can, too...

343
00:18:38.980 --> 00:18:40.100
With those boots.

344
00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:43.260
Your dumb shoes
are just like mine.

345
00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:44.800
They have a hover function.

346
00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:45.750
Really?

347
00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:47.350
How do we use it?

348
00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:48.320
Ah, tell us!

349
00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.620
Press the little
button on the side.

350
00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:59.500
And next, take this lever
and push it down, like so.

351
00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:02.270
Very good!

352
00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.940
Oh!

353
00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.470
<b>The World's Premier Brain</b>

354
00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:28.900
<b>The World's Premier Brain</b>

355
00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:28.900
<b>Head of the Marines' Special Science Group</b>
